    "summary": "Tight June ’73 set shines with Dark Star → Eyes → Stella, vibrant Bird Song",
    "blurb": "The Universal Amphitheatre show delivers a soaring Dark Star into Eyes of the World and Stella Blue, plus a beautifully rendered Bird Song. Jerry’s vocals and lead work are on point while Phil lays down deep, warm bass throughout. Soundboard and matrix sources capture the band in tight, high‑energy form.",
    "review": "June 30, 1973 at the Universal Amphitheatre finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. The first set rolls through classics – The Promised Land, They Love Each Other, and a punchy Playing In The Band that tees up one of the night’s highlights: a seamless segue into Dark Star. From there the band launches an expansive Dark Star → Eyes Of The World → Stella Blue suite that many reviewers call “monster‑level,” with Jerry’s soaring leads, Phil’s booming low end, Keith’s sweet Rhodes textures and Bill’s crisp drumming all locked in tight groove. Bird Song shines mid‑set, its lyrical phrasing buoyed by a melodic piano weave, while the second set builds momentum with The Greatest Story Ever Told, Ramble On Rose and a bright Sugar Magnolia finale that leaves the audience buzzing. Across the best matrix mix (gd1973-06-30.sbd.sbvol9.chappell.29753.flac16) the instruments sit cleanly in the mix, preserving the live energy without sacrificing clarity, making this one of the standout 1973 recordings.",
